   "statspai_version": "1.43.1",
   "mechanism": "Known property of the method, documented in sp.dose_response. The Hirano-Imbens estimator regresses the outcome on the dose and the generalized propensity score and is consistent only if that regression is right. Here the outcome model is linear in (T, GPS). The GPS is a normal density of the treatment residual, an even function of it, so it is uncorrelated with a covariate that enters the outcome linearly and the fitted curve keeps the unadjusted slope 0.7 + 0.5 / 1.25 = 1.1 instead of 0.7. The standard error is right for that estimate (SE / SD 0.94); the interval is centred in the wrong place. The docstring reports the same bias for the Hirano-Imbens quadratic and the function warns on its default models; method='dr' is unbiased on this design (dose_response.dr). When the covariates move the dose only, the GPS path is in band (dose_response.gps)."
  },
